# SPA fallback: every client-side route (/templates, /templates/jack, /projects…)
# must serve index.html so React Router can handle it on a direct load or refresh.
#
# This file is the PORTABLE version of the redirect in netlify.toml. Netlify,
# Cloudflare Pages and Render all read _redirects, so the site can move between
# hosts without its routes 404ing. On Netlify the netlify.toml rule wins and
# this is simply ignored — keeping both costs nothing and means one less thing
# to remember when switching host.
/*    /index.html   200
